ng ramps up through October, or whether Kansas's late-deciding voters revert to form as they have in past cycles.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Roger Marshall (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kansas has not elected a Democratic senator in more than ninety years, and Republican Roger Marshall is seeking a second term with an eight-point partisan lean and a substantial cash advantage in his corner. Yet recent polls from across the sponsor spectrum show the race dead even: Trafalgar and New York Times/Siena found a tie in late September, while Emerson and Democratic-sponsored surveys gave challenger Adam Hamilton a two-point edge.\n\nHamilton, a Republican-turned-Democrat and prominent pastor, has matched Marshall in fundraising and drawn endorsements from former GOP governors. Republican outside groups have moved money into Kansas from North Carolina, a sign of worry. Expert ratings split between Lean R and Tossup, and prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-three chance. The seat stays slightly favored to remain Republican, but a real upset is in play.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2893, "margin": -2.76}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3585, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.4222, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4301, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3024, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2988, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4183, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.4225, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.3457, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4294, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3861, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3969, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4021, "margin": -1.8}]}